    "result_text": "The project has a single test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented membership level 4 gated on tenure.\n\n**`Owner.getMembershipLevel()`** (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`) \u2014 after computing the pre-tenure level (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for zero namesakes, capped at 3), it now awards a fourth level when tenure exceeds 365 days:\n\n```java\nlevel = Math.min(level, 3);\nif (this.registrationDate != null\n    && java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(this.registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365) {\n    level++;\n}\nreturn level;\n```\n\nTenure is the whole days from `registrationDate` to today. A newly created owner has `registrationDate` set to today (zero tenure), so it can never reach level 4 \u2014 a new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` 0, and a 3-member household lands at level 3, exactly as the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test asserts.\n\nI also updated the Javadoc and the `openapi.yml` schema (description + `maximum: 4`) to document the 1\u20134 range.\n\nBoth the new acceptance test and the full suite pass.",
